## Phase 2 — VBA Extraction & Macro-Mutated Cell Census (.xlsm only)

### 2.1 Export VBA source

Requires the Excel Trust Center setting **"Trust access to the VBA project object
model"**. If the export throws, report the exact setting path
(File → Options → Trust Center → Trust Center Settings → Macro Settings) and stop this
sub-phase — do not guess at module contents.

```powershell
# ExportVBA.ps1 -Workbook <path> -OutDir <dir>
param([Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Workbook,
      [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$OutDir)
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
$excel = New-Object -ComObject Excel.Application
$excel.Visible = $false; $excel.DisplayAlerts = $false
$excel.EnableEvents = $false                       # block Workbook_Open
try {
    $wb = $excel.Workbooks.Open((Resolve-Path $Workbook).Path, 0, $true)  # read-only
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $OutDir | Out-Null
    foreach ($comp in $wb.VBProject.VBComponents) {
        $ext = switch ($comp.Type) { 1 {".bas"} 2 {".cls"} 3 {".frm"} default {".cls"} }
        $comp.Export((Join-Path (Resolve-Path $OutDir).Path ($comp.Name + $ext)))
        Write-Output "exported: $($comp.Name)$ext"
    }
    $wb.Close($false)
}
finally { $excel.Quit()
    [void][Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ReleaseComObject($excel) }
```

Exported `.bas/.cls/.frm` files go under version control next to the workbook. This is
what lets Copilot read business logic that lives in code, and what makes VBA changes
diffable in PRs.

### 2.2 Macro-mutated cell census

Scan exported source for worksheet writes — these cells hold values **no formula
explains**, and a pure formula graph silently lies about them:

```
Patterns: Range("...").Value / .Value2 / .Formula =,  Cells(r,c) =,
          [A1] =,  .Offset(...).Value =,  Named-range writes
```

Produce `out/macro_mutated_cells.md`: a table of `Module.Procedure → target
(sheet/range/named range) → static or computed target`. Computed targets (variables in
`Range(var)`) are reported as **unresolvable macro writes** and treated like opaque refs.
Also census **UDFs** (`Public Function` used in any worksheet formula — cross-reference
against Phase 3 graph): these require macros enabled during recalc (Principle 7).

