## Phase 3 — Dependency Graph & Blast Radius

```bash
python scripts/xl_engine.py graph   workbook.xlsm --out out/graph.json
python scripts/xl_engine.py mermaid workbook.xlsm > out/flow.mermaid
python scripts/xl_engine.py blast   workbook.xlsm "Assumptions!B14"
```

- **`graph.json`** — cell-level `precedents` and `dependents` adjacency. Named ranges are
  resolved through to their underlying cells; ranges expand up to 10,000 cells (beyond
  that, a single range-node preserves correctness without exploding memory).
- **`flow.mermaid`** — sheet-level aggregation (`Assumptions -->|4 refs| Calc`) for the
  human-readable overview.
- **`blast`** — transitive dependents of one or more seed cells/names. This is the answer
  to *"what happens if I change this?"* — e.g.
  `{"seeds": ["Assumptions!B2"], "count": 6, "affected": ["Calc!A1", ...]}`.

Cells flagged in Phase 2.2 as macro-mutated are annotated in graph output consumers:
any blast radius touching a macro-mutated cell must carry the warning
*"downstream values partially produced by VBA — formula graph incomplete here."*

