## Phase 4 — Golden-Master Baseline

The baseline is the reference truth every future change is diffed against. It is valid
**only** if produced by this procedure:

```powershell
# GoldenMaster.ps1 -Workbook <path> -Out <snapshot.json>
param([Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Workbook,
      [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Out)
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
function ColName([int]$n){ $s=""; while($n){ $n--; $s=[char](65+($n%26))+$s; $n=[int][math]::Floor($n/26)}; $s }
$excel = New-Object -ComObject Excel.Application
$excel.Visible = $false; $excel.DisplayAlerts = $false
$excel.EnableEvents = $false                    # block auto-run events
$excel.AutomationSecurity = 1                   # msoAutomationSecurityLow: UDFs must work (Principle 7)
try {
    $wb = $excel.Workbooks.Open((Resolve-Path $Workbook).Path, 0, $true)   # no link update, read-only
    $excel.CalculateFullRebuild()
    while ($excel.CalculationState -ne 0) { Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }
    $snap = [ordered]@{}; $errCount = 0
    foreach ($ws in $wb.Worksheets) {
        $used = $ws.UsedRange
        if ($null -eq $used) { continue }
        # Two bulk COM calls per sheet — never iterate cells over COM (orders of magnitude slower)
        $vals = $used.Value2; $fmls = $used.Formula
        $r0 = $used.Row; $c0 = $used.Column
        $nr = $used.Rows.Count; $nc = $used.Columns.Count
        try { $errCount += $used.SpecialCells(-4123, 16).Count } catch { }  # formulas -> errors
        for ($r = 1; $r -le $nr; $r++) {
            for ($c = 1; $c -le $nc; $c++) {
                if ($nr -eq 1 -and $nc -eq 1) { $v = $vals; $f = $fmls }
                else { $v = $vals[$r, $c]; $f = $fmls[$r, $c] }
                $isF = ($f -is [string] -and $f.StartsWith("="))
                if ($null -eq $v -and -not $isF) { continue }
                $key = "$($ws.Name)!$(ColName ($c0+$c-1))$($r0+$r-1)"
                $snap[$key] = @{ f = $(if ($isF) { $f.Substring(1) } else { $null })   # strip '=' to match XML form
                                 v = $(if ($null -ne $v) { "$v" } else { $null }) }
            }
        }
    }
    @{ meta = @{ source = "CalculateFullRebuild"; workbook = (Split-Path $Workbook -Leaf)
                 timestamp = (Get-Date -Format o); error_cells = $errCount }
       cells = $snap } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 4 -Compress | Set-Content $Out -Encoding UTF8
    Write-Output "baseline: $($snap.Count) cells, $errCount error cells -> $Out"
    $wb.Close($false)
}
finally { $excel.Quit()
    [void][Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ReleaseComObject($excel) }
```

Baseline rules:

- **Staleness detection:** independently run `xl_engine.py snapshot` (raw cached values)
  and diff against the COM baseline. Non-trivial differences prove the file was saved
  stale — record this in the report; it is itself a finding about the workbook's hygiene.
- **`meta.error_cells`** is the error floor. Any change that increases it fails the gate.
- **Iterative calculation ON** (`calcPr.iterate="1"`): circular models may not converge
  to bit-identical values. Run the baseline **twice**; the observed baseline-to-baseline
  drift defines the minimum diff tolerance, recorded in the report. If drift exceeds the
  business-acceptable tolerance, escalate to the user before any modification.
- **Designated entry-point macros:** if the user names macros that populate results
  (e.g. `RunModel`), a second baseline variant is captured post-macro-run
  (`$excel.Run("RunModel")` before snapshotting). Never auto-discover and run macros.

