## Phase 5 — Change Protocol (the core loop)

Every modification — formula edit, assumption update, business-logic change — follows
these steps **in order**. No skipping.

```
1. DECLARE   Change intent: cells/names to modify, expected value deltas (if known)
2. PREDICT   blast <seeds>  ->  predicted blast radius R  (report count + sheets touched)
3. BACKUP    Copy-Item workbook.xlsm workbook.backup-<yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>.xlsm
4. BASELINE  GoldenMaster.ps1 -> before.json   (skip only if a current certified baseline exists)
5. APPLY     ApplyChange.ps1  (COM edit — never raw XML surgery on .xlsm)
6. RECALC+   GoldenMaster.ps1 -> after.json    (against the modified file)
7. DIFF      xl_engine.py diff before.json after.json --exclude <nondeterministic_cells>
8. GATE      Evaluate (below)
9. VERDICT   Accept (report) or REVERT from backup (report why)
```

```powershell
# ApplyChange.ps1 -Workbook <path> -Changes <changes.json>
# changes.json: [ { "cell": "Assumptions!B14", "formula": "=B12*1.07" },
#                 { "cell": "Assumptions!B2",  "value": 250 } ]
param([Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Workbook,
      [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Changes)
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
$list = Get-Content $Changes -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$excel = New-Object -ComObject Excel.Application
$excel.Visible = $false; $excel.DisplayAlerts = $false
$excel.EnableEvents = $false; $excel.AutomationSecurity = 1
try {
    $wb = $excel.Workbooks.Open((Resolve-Path $Workbook).Path, 0, $false)
    foreach ($ch in $list) {
        $sheet, $addr = $ch.cell -split "!", 2
        $rng = $wb.Worksheets.Item($sheet).Range($addr)
        if ($null -ne $ch.formula) { $rng.Formula = $ch.formula }
        elseif ($null -ne $ch.value) { $rng.Value2 = $ch.value }
        Write-Output "applied: $($ch.cell)"
    }
    $excel.CalculateFullRebuild()
    while ($excel.CalculationState -ne 0) { Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }
    $wb.Save(); $wb.Close($true)
}
finally { $excel.Quit()
    [void][Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ReleaseComObject($excel) }
```

### The gate (step 8)

| Check | Rule | On failure |
|---|---|---|
| **Intended edits present** | Every declared change appears in the diff exactly as intended | REVERT |
| **Containment** | Every *other* diff entry ∈ predicted blast radius R | REVERT + report escapees with formulas |
| **Error floor** | `after.meta.error_cells ≤ before.meta.error_cells` | REVERT |
| **Tolerance** | Numeric diffs use `rel_tol=1e-9, abs_tol=1e-12` (or the iterative-calc drift floor from Phase 4) | flag, human decides |
| **Nondeterministic exclusion** | `NOW/TODAY/RAND*` cells excluded via `--exclude` | n/a (mandatory setup) |

**Containment downgrade rule:** if Phase 1 found `opaque_ref_cells > 0` on any sheet the
diff touches, the containment check is downgraded to **advisory** (static graphs cannot
see through `INDIRECT`/`OFFSET`). The verdict then rests on: intended edits + error floor
+ human review of each out-of-radius diff entry, presented with before/after formulas
and values. State this downgrade explicitly in the verdict — never present advisory
containment as a hard guarantee.

### Verdict format (evidence-only)

```
CHANGE VERDICT: ACCEPTED
Intent:      Assumptions!B14  =B12*1.05 -> =B12*1.07
Predicted:   47 dependents across [Calc, Summary, Dashboard]
Observed:    31 value diffs, all ∈ predicted radius; 0 formula diffs beyond intent
Error floor: 0 -> 0
Excluded:    Calc!C1 (NOW), Dashboard!F2 (TODAY)
Backup:      workbook.backup-20260706-143012.xlsm (retained)
```

