## Fidelity Ledger

| Decision | Status | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Python/JS formula re-evaluation | **REJECTED** | No implementation reaches full Excel semantics (dates, precision, implicit intersection, dynamic arrays). Partial fidelity is worse than none for "must not go wrong" workloads. |
| LibreOffice headless recalc | **REJECTED** for .xlsm | Function-level result divergences; known risk of VBA project damage on save. |
| Raw XML surgery on .xlsm | **REJECTED** for writes | Shared-formula tables, calc chain part, and VBA-adjacent parts make hand-edits corruption-prone. Reads via XML are fine; writes go through COM only. |
| Static resolution of `INDIRECT`/`OFFSET` | **NOT POSSIBLE** | Runtime-computed references. Mitigated by containment downgrade rule + diff gate. |
| VBA runtime behavior verification | **PARTIAL** | Structural census only, plus baselines for user-designated entry macros. Arbitrary macro behavior is not exercised. |
| Nondeterministic functions in diffs | **EXCLUDED** | `NOW/TODAY/RAND*` diffs carry no regression signal. Exclusion list is auto-derived (Phase 1), never hand-maintained. |
| External link values | **FROZEN** | Opened with no link update; boundary values are those cached at baseline time. Refresh is an explicit, user-approved operation. |
| Excel COM scripts | **RUNTIME-CERTIFIED** | Authored on Linux without Excel; Phase 0.1 smoke test certifies them on the target machine before first use. The Python engine (Appendix A) is live-verified 9/9 in the authoring environment. |

---

## Hard Aborts

- Phase 0.2 < 9/9 → **stop everything**
- Phase 0.1 fails → analysis-only mode; refuse modification requests with the reason
- `CalculationState` never reaches done within timeout (default 10 min) → kill Excel
  process, report; suspect runaway iterative calc or external-link stall
- Diff gate containment failure → **automatic revert from backup**, then report
- Workbook is password-protected / opened by another process → stop, ask user
- User requests a change to a cell inside an unresolvable macro-write target → refuse
  the automated path; require the VBA change route (edit exported module, human review,
  re-import) instead

